          "land_swap": false,
          "open_space_designation": "Local Open Spaces",
          "description": "While the spectator area and wellness room introduce small scale built form to the open space, these directly support the wider sporting use of the site. Both facilities provide much needed facilities to support players, with the wellness room providing a space for players to undertake strength training and conditioning in preparation for matches or to recover post-match, while the spectator area allows visitors/ coaches to safely watch matches, coaching sessions and community events. The site is predominantly comprised of hardstanding associated with its wider sporting use. The area now used for the spectator area was previously solely used as an access route to the northern courts. Access to and from the northern courts can still be gained via the doors at either end of the spectator shelter. The area now used as the wellness room replaces a pre‑existing storage unit of a similar scale within a triangular corner of the site not suitable for sporting use. Both sites can therefore be considered to have made a minimal contribution to the open space designation, while their current use enhances the quality of the facilities available for players, supporting the sporting use of the site. \n",
          "open_space_type": "Non-residential institution grounds or garden"
